This benchmark draws on prior work as follows. No source code from the projects below is included
unless stated; the driver, adapters and page are original work under Apache-2.0.

1. ClickBench (https://github.com/ClickHouse/ClickBench), CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0: the runner shape (one
   directory per system with install/start/stop/check/load scripts), the tuning rules for participants,
   the relative-coloured result table and the geometric-mean ranking. Design pattern only.

2. SearchBench (https://github.com/serenedb/searchbench), Apache-2.0: the adapter contract, the
   results-file-per-engine layout and the React frontend architecture, from which parts of
   frontend/ are adapted.

3. ann-benchmarks (https://github.com/erikbern/ann-benchmarks), MIT, and big-ann-benchmarks
   (https://github.com/harsha-simhadri/big-ann-benchmarks), MIT: the recall-versus-throughput frontier
   reading, the tie-aware recall definition and the dataset conventions. Ideas only.

4. Qdrant's ann-filtering-benchmark-datasets (https://github.com/qdrant/ann-filtering-benchmark-datasets)
   and VectorDBBench (https://github.com/zilliztech/VectorDBBench): filter selectivity ladders and
   filtered-search methodology. Ideas only.

Datasets are downloaded by `vectorbench prepare` from their publishers and are not part of this
repository: BIGANN/SIFT (INRIA, big-ann-benchmarks distribution), Cohere Wikipedia embeddings
(Hugging Face, Apache-2.0 dataset card over CC-BY-SA Wikipedia text). Each family's yml names its
source; check the publisher's terms before redistributing prepared data.
